window.docContents[122].resolve({"/UD-VI___-type-systems/#Core-C______--UD-VI___-type-systems":{"contents":"Overloading of functions and methods by the type of the arguments, operator members, class templates instantiated by substitution, subtyping and type inference. A name denotes an overload set, and a call selects one candidate. An infix operator on an object, and the indexing of an object, are the calls of the members operator⊕ and operator[], and a member may return , which is what makes v[i] = x work. A template is expanded before the program is checked, so instantiation costs nothing at run time and a template is never checked, only its instantiations are.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Core C++","header":"7. UD VI, type systems","id":"/UD-VI___-type-systems/#Core-C______--UD-VI___-type-systems"}});